# Notebook outputs are stripped on the way into git by a `clean` filter, so the
# working copy keeps its figures and animations while the committed blob does
# not. The filter lives in analyses/tools/strip_animation_outputs.py.
#
# Filters are configured in .git/config, which is NOT committed, so each clone
# must run once:
#
#     ./analyses/tools/install_git_filters.sh
#
# Until it is run, this line is inert and notebooks are committed as-is.
*.ipynb filter=nbstrip diff=ipynb
